Dear Sir or Madam,

Swansea City Association Football Club (Swansea City AFC) is pleased to sup=
port Dr Rowan Brown's application to the EPSRC Mathematical Sciences Small =
Grants scheme.

Commitment. If the award is made, Swansea City AFC will support the twelve-=
month project as a project partner. Support is in kind. There is no cash co=
ntribution. The club will provide access to Championship tracking data and =
tactical labels through its commercial data agreement, and will take part i=
n scheduled co-development reviews with the university team. Should funding=
 be awarded, we will enter into a formal collaboration agreement with Swans=
ea University as required for UKRI audit.

Value to Swansea City AFC. The project will deliver checkable structural me=
asures of pressing, formation gaps and defensive-line organisation, develop=
ed against our matches and footage. These outputs are not available from co=
nventional geometric descriptors such as team length, width or convex-hull =
area. They will give our performance and analysis staff quantifiable, scale=
-specific summaries of collective organisation that can be checked against =
the match.

Value Swansea City AFC brings. The club brings the production tracking feed=
 required for both project objectives, formation and phase-of-play labels, =
and coach- and analyst-facing checks that the mathematical summaries name r=
eal organisational states. We also bring an established research relationsh=
ip with Swansea University, including co-investment in doctoral training, w=
hich supports efficient delivery within the twelve-month award.

We confirm that this partnership is relevant to our performance analysis pr=
ogramme and that we are willing to act as the sole industry project partner=
 for the application named above.

